    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1155">

                <pb facs="1173" n="887" xml:id="pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/62b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-26T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2945. There is a strong feeling here of sympathy for the destitute in Poland, and
                    an increasing demand that relief should be sent to them. To all inquiries
                    Department advises that Hoover is now
                    endeavoring to secure the necessary permission to extend over Poland
                    organization of the Belgian Relief Commission, and that when this is
                    accomplished, as it is hoped it will be, relief can go forward from this
                    country. If you see no objection, you may advise Sir
                        Edward Grey of the anxiety of large numbers of American citizens
                    and of their desire to send assistance to the destitute in Poland. See
                    Department’s 2926, 23d, and inform Hoover
                    prompt reply requested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
